--- page 264 ----------------------------------------------------
in the Southern region have been circumcised, as compared with 77% in the Islands region and 67% in
the Momase region. Approximately 3 in 10 men in the Southern region were circumcised by a
traditional practitioner, friend, or family member, compared with 68% of men in the Islands region.
▪ The percentage of men who have been circumcised varies by province, from 20% in Milne Bay to
91% in West New Britain.
▪ There are notable variations in the prevalence of circumcision by religion. The proportion of men who
have been circumcised is highest among those who are Roman Catholics (58%) and lowest among
those who are Evangelical Alliance and United Church members (40% each).

